[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1109","stub":{"id":"1109","section":"0.7 Iron Duff to Fines Creek ","altname":"Hepco Run","river":"Pigeon","difficulty":"IIIplus","states":["USA-NCR"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"233","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:30:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"This well-established pull-off appears to be public land (DOT) on the County GIS maps.","id":"109309","location":{"latitude":"35.600772","longitude":"-82.950866"},"name":"Crabtree Creek Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"A great surf wave and fun rapid that you miss if you paddle Jonathan's Creek into the run.","id":"RXd1Jb4i60YzrylNbZETE","location":{"latitude":"35.625211","longitude":"-82.994904"},"name":"Earn Your Surf","distance":"3.48","difficulty":"III-","approximate":false,"photoID":"uYibDPoemEkWr3TZYAj01"},{"type":"rapid","description":"One of 5-6 nice class III rapids in the second half of the Hepco Run, and often the most challenging.\n\nThis rapid can be run in several ways. There is a center slot which you can enter with some left boat angle and then exit the rapid in the main flow. There is a boulder in the center of the flow so you'll have to make a choice when you approach it. There are two left entrances, one that takes you far left or you enter on your right edge and it shoots you into the center current. Avoid the far right side of this rapid as there is a dangerous undercut on the right. If unsure, scout on the right bank.","id":"UJQQhDBkIa6w3mFs4RYfN","location":{"latitude":"35.648074","longitude":"-82.995087"},"name":"Wormy's","distance":"5.68","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"jqGkoe3wmgadkKFQ2tEAH"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Keep'er sunnyside up on this wave because its shallow, but the polished sloping bedrock beneath the wave gives it a great shape.","id":"KUbxQzdOieziKgz1yQKxy","location":{"latitude":"35.651786","longitude":"-82.99466"},"name":"Sunnyside Wave","distance":"5.95","difficulty":"III-","approximate":false,"photoID":"RK8H3H0um651qgDotGFp4"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Just picking a random name for a fun rapid run down the tongue. There is a large white rock upstream on river left. Rename this if it has a real name!","id":"Usdm0mbsED13ZNkTefa4W","location":{"latitude":"35.655209","longitude":"-82.992438"},"name":"White Rock Rapid ","distance":"6.24","difficulty":"III-","approximate":false,"photoID":"v3HlfGYrSfIYcPlcekhjm"},{"type":"rapid","description":"The old dam has at least a couple lines, and can also be walked on and scouted on river right.\n\nPost-Helene, this is the rapid that has changed the most on the Hepco section. It is boat-scoutable, and there are eddies between each drop. The dam is short and still runnable on the right, while the left side is easily runnable. The preferred line in the second drop is the center, pointing right, into the eddy. The last drop has a tongue in the center, which leads to a left line and avoids a hole. This is more favorable than the right side along the wall, as there is a giant hole at the bottom (1550 cfs). The right side may be fine at lower levels.","id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","location":{"latitude":"35.659933","longitude":"-82.989313"},"name":"Old Hepco Dam","distance":"6.63","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"ccdbsZWw4HJWrWQf61DvC"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Following Helene, The rapid below Hepco Dam might merit status as a separate rapid given the new big eddy/pool between the two drops. This one packs a big punch at higher water!","id":"93vH6X87ktrYXDMPbifP5","location":{"latitude":"35.660466","longitude":"-82.989119"},"name":"Finale Below Hepco Dam Rapid","distance":"6.66","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"kyDvUB1w9GYWgFpNTexIp"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Take out on river left just past the bridge and walk up to a gravel pull off. Not recommended for rafts. This is a relatively short but steep hike up to the parking, but the trail is well established.","id":"114551","location":{"latitude":"35.66478777","longitude":"-82.99500209"},"name":"Fines Creek Rd Take Out","distance":"7.18","photoID":"9TslLWwfVjwXc22ZaAU98","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"qznFWAdYSxFQcHeY6h9bi","ext":"jpg","post_id":"szwW379cuV5bwnaGswvpC","description":"The river was only moderately impacted by Helene, mostly by debris, but this landslide/erosion is one of several areas like this that dot the run. ","caption":"Jonathan's Confluence Bank Carving","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"vGeIhzeyzyFICCXE3CKLt","photo_date":"2025-02-23T13:05:50.000Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T13:05:50.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/qznFWAdYSxFQcHeY6h9bi","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/qznFWAdYSxFQcHeY6h9bi"}},{"id":"90msTW6aiKhIAt931vewL","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"This old broken dam can be run on the right or left, and also easily walked on the right. The holes can get big. ","caption":"Hepco Dam","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/90msTW6aiKhIAt931vewL","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/90msTW6aiKhIAt931vewL"}},{"id":"RK8H3H0um651qgDotGFp4","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"This wave was shallow but had a great shape, and eddy access. ","caption":"Nice surf wave","poi_name":null,"subject":"Jack Henderson","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/RK8H3H0um651qgDotGFp4","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/RK8H3H0um651qgDotGFp4"}},{"id":"aFigJUVu4sahIfGuHtjAh","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"There were at least a half dozen great surf waves on the run at this level, generally with eddy access. ","caption":"More great surf","poi_name":null,"subject":"Jack Henderson","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/aFigJUVu4sahIfGuHtjAh","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/aFigJUVu4sahIfGuHtjAh"}},{"id":"uYibDPoemEkWr3TZYAj01","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"Paddling Jonathans Creek into the Hepco run skips this fun wave/rapid upstream of the confluence.","caption":"Great surf upstream of Jonathans","poi_name":null,"subject":"Jack Henderson","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/uYibDPoemEkWr3TZYAj01","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/uYibDPoemEkWr3TZYAj01"}},{"id":"cZaM9rRHehfclPeTtfUpe","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"Typical rapid on the Hepco run. ","caption":"A fun one!","poi_name":null,"subject":"Jack Henderson","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/cZaM9rRHehfclPeTtfUpe","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/cZaM9rRHehfclPeTtfUpe"}},{"id":"BjWARcgQ3MUZil7CnOsYN","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"","caption":"Run out of a bigger one","poi_name":null,"subject":"Jack Henderson","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-25T23:11:45.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/BjWARcgQ3MUZil7CnOsYN","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/BjWARcgQ3MUZil7CnOsYN"}},{"id":"9OIyfXXnzw86z34mGcDZY","ext":"jpg","post_id":"XmwWb9il4EmZxfCxdqNEh","description":"","caption":"Hole on river right of the biggest rapid other than the dam","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-03-25T13:39:07.000Z","updated_at":"2023-03-27T13:39:07.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9OIyfXXnzw86z34mGcDZY","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9OIyfXXnzw86z34mGcDZY"}},{"id":"pj1M7IRryUEeWQSrvN1ra","ext":"jpg","post_id":"7CJ4iKxP9wyjhiL3blH0f","description":"","caption":"Earn your Surf 2.14.25","poi_name":null,"subject":"Fantastic surf at this level, good eddy access from river right. Shallow immediately behind, so roll up quick if you flip.","author":"Mitchell Bearden","poi_id":"RXd1Jb4i60YzrylNbZETE","photo_date":"2025-02-14T14:47:40.000Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T14:47:40.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/pj1M7IRryUEeWQSrvN1ra","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/pj1M7IRryUEeWQSrvN1ra"}},{"id":"9TslLWwfVjwXc22ZaAU98","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"Lots of roadside parking for the take-out. ","caption":"Parking at the Take-Out","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"114551","photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:47.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/9TslLWwfVjwXc22ZaAU98","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/9TslLWwfVjwXc22ZaAU98"}},{"id":"e67id7Lk6Zl2QVNcdRDsa","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"At low flows booting the dam is pretty chill. ","caption":"Boofing the Dam","poi_name":null,"subject":"Evan","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:47.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/e67id7Lk6Zl2QVNcdRDsa","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/e67id7Lk6Zl2QVNcdRDsa"}},{"id":"XhKqgVYNQdzxcBKNy6Jel","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"This was the best wave on the river at 450, located downstream of the Dam a rapid or two. ","caption":"A Sweet Low Water Wave","poi_name":null,"subject":"Evan","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:47.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/XhKqgVYNQdzxcBKNy6Jel","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/XhKqgVYNQdzxcBKNy6Jel"}},{"id":"mdzYuN0VWE4Z9W8EhX0kf","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"The hole is low key at these flows (450)","caption":"Brian Boofing the Dam","poi_name":null,"subject":"Brian Byrd","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:47.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/mdzYuN0VWE4Z9W8EhX0kf","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/mdzYuN0VWE4Z9W8EhX0kf"}},{"id":"xykaBw8yUbfATODhTdd5e","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"This wave was not nearly as nice at 450 as it was at 950, but it still was fun to surf. ","caption":"Low Water Sunnyside","poi_name":null,"subject":"Evan","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"KUbxQzdOieziKgz1yQKxy","photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:47.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/xykaBw8yUbfATODhTdd5e","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/xykaBw8yUbfATODhTdd5e"}},{"id":"kk7cEPvzIAJotSbvw3KJe","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"Always fun to paddle two rivers in one trip! ","caption":"Jonathan's Creek Confluence","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"vGeIhzeyzyFICCXE3CKLt","photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:47.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/kk7cEPvzIAJotSbvw3KJe","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/kk7cEPvzIAJotSbvw3KJe"}},{"id":"WVWjlQuQ2SQvqIzazk94D","ext":"jpg","post_id":"gwjmUBqIS8BZNQGLvX7sy","description":"This slot on the right side of Island was a mess of pin rocks and wood at 450. We ran a slot further left. ","caption":"Right Side of Island","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"UJQQhDBkIa6w3mFs4RYfN","photo_date":"2023-12-03T16:51:47.000Z","updated_at":"2023-12-04T16:51:48.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/WVWjlQuQ2SQvqIzazk94D","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/WVWjlQuQ2SQvqIzazk94D"}},{"id":"su3D2de4UguLsB6ie02os","ext":"jpg","post_id":"plB4oOFWU7c2mpshYpuOc","description":"","caption":"Fun Wave to Rally Through","poi_name":null,"subject":"Dan","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2024-01-11T14:48:24.000Z","updated_at":"2024-01-12T14:48:24.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/su3D2de4UguLsB6ie02os","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/su3D2de4UguLsB6ie02os"}},{"id":"P2SJXZLr9Ik1J4CWUiJyb","ext":"jpg","post_id":"7CJ4iKxP9wyjhiL3blH0f","description":"","caption":"Bottom of Hepco Dam","poi_name":null,"subject":"Right side is the best line at this level. Fairly large hole in the bottom.","author":"Mitchell Bearden","poi_id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","photo_date":"2025-02-14T14:47:40.000Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T14:47:40.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/P2SJXZLr9Ik1J4CWUiJyb","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/P2SJXZLr9Ik1J4CWUiJyb"}},{"id":"DTDICWpn80QK2aI6X9Wv7","ext":"jpg","post_id":"7CJ4iKxP9wyjhiL3blH0f","description":"","caption":"Bottom of Hepco Dam - Right line","poi_name":null,"subject":"Following the tongue into the top wave. If you hit it right, you can thread the needle between the two bottom holes.","author":"Mitchell Bearden","poi_id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","photo_date":"2025-02-14T14:47:40.000Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T14:47:40.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/DTDICWpn80QK2aI6X9Wv7","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/DTDICWpn80QK2aI6X9Wv7"}},{"id":"ccdbsZWw4HJWrWQf61DvC","ext":"jpg","post_id":"szwW379cuV5bwnaGswvpC","description":"Clean lines down river left, big eddies, and a fun boof in the second drop. Quite different, but fun! ","caption":"Post-Helene Hepco Dam Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":"Evan and Dup","author":"Kevin Colburn","poi_id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","photo_date":"2025-02-23T13:05:50.000Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T13:05:50.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/ccdbsZWw4HJWrWQf61DvC","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/ccdbsZWw4HJWrWQf61DvC"}},{"id":"3ijeCtBbdhPNSXAqMpOGK","ext":"jpg","post_id":"7CJ4iKxP9wyjhiL3blH0f","description":"","caption":"Middle Drop of Hepco Dam","poi_name":null,"subject":"Scout from top right, a few lines to choose from through the top two drops","author":"Mitchell Bearden","poi_id":"4w9BJsLGu4viEAqBPhCRX","photo_date":"2025-02-14T14:47:40.000Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T14:47:40.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3ijeCtBbdhPNSXAqMpOGK","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3ijeCtBbdhPNSXAqMpOGK"}},{"id":"6WehcqTYmerf8WhR6duAk","ext":"jpg","post_id":"szwW379cuV5bwnaGswvpC","description":"","caption":"Surfing","poi_name":null,"subjec